1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:03,398
A search product says it uses vectors.

2
00:00:03,561 --> 00:00:04,597
What does that tell you?

3
00:00:04,785 --> 00:00:07,265
Before answering, look at three ordinary

4
00:00:07,285 --> 00:00:08,592
keyword records.

5
00:00:08,767 --> 00:00:10,241
Heart attack treatment.

6
00:00:10,416 --> 00:00:11,684
Job interview tips.

7
00:00:11,847 --> 00:00:12,986
Cancer treatment.

8
00:00:13,161 --> 00:00:15,551
We can turn every one into a vector

9
00:00:15,571 --> 00:00:17,909
without training a neural network.

10
00:00:18,071 --> 00:00:19,662
Make a prediction: what will the

11
00:00:19,682 --> 00:00:20,911
coordinates mean?

12
00:00:23,348 --> 00:00:25,413
They will mean vocabulary terms.

13
00:00:25,589 --> 00:00:28,069
Vector names a numerical object: an

14
00:00:28,089 --> 00:00:29,756
ordered list of numbers.

15
00:00:29,931 --> 00:00:32,360
Chapter Eight makes those hidden choices

16
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:33,197
visible.

17
00:00:34,127 --> 00:00:37,638
Fix this vocabulary order: attack, cancer,

18
00:00:37,671 --> 00:00:41,065
heart, interview, job, tips, treatment.

19
00:00:41,202 --> 00:00:44,571
Every document now lives in the same seven

20
00:00:44,591 --> 00:00:45,949
dimensional space.

21
00:00:46,125 --> 00:00:48,733
Coordinate three always means heart.

22
00:00:49,297 --> 00:00:52,447
Put one where a term occurs and zero where

23
00:00:52,467 --> 00:00:54,779
it does not. The first document activates

24
00:00:54,799 --> 00:00:56,918
attack, heart and treatment.

25
00:00:57,080 --> 00:00:59,547
The second activates interview, job and

26
00:00:59,567 --> 00:01:02,563
tips. The third activates cancer and

27
00:01:02,583 --> 00:01:05,385
treatment. These are sparse, vocabulary

28
00:01:05,405 --> 00:01:06,660
aligned vectors.

29
00:01:07,569 --> 00:01:09,147
Now search for heart treatment.

30
00:01:09,322 --> 00:01:11,738
Its two active coordinates overlap the

31
00:01:11,758 --> 00:01:15,011
first document twice, the third once, and

32
00:01:15,031 --> 00:01:16,376
the second not at all.

33
00:01:16,526 --> 00:01:19,160
Counting shared ones gives a graded score.

34
00:01:19,708 --> 00:01:22,464
Heart AND treatment admits only the first

35
00:01:22,484 --> 00:01:25,415
document. Heart OR treatment admits the

36
00:01:25,435 --> 00:01:26,896
first and third.

37
00:01:27,084 --> 00:01:29,822
The binary vector did not contain either

38
00:01:29,842 --> 00:01:32,618
operator. The retrieval rule decides

39
00:01:32,638 --> 00:01:34,822
whether term evidence becomes a hard

40
00:01:34,842 --> 00:01:36,742
requirement or a contribution to a

41
00:01:36,762 --> 00:01:37,489
ranking.

42
00:01:38,417 --> 00:01:41,102
Change the first document to heart attack

43
00:01:41,122 --> 00:01:42,712
treatment treatment treatment.

44
00:01:42,888 --> 00:01:46,115
Binary presence barely notices: the same

45
00:01:46,135 --> 00:01:48,344
three coordinates are active.

46
00:01:48,519 --> 00:01:51,747
Raw term frequency instead puts three in

47
00:01:51,767 --> 00:01:53,202
the treatment coordinate.

48
00:01:53,377 --> 00:01:55,741
The vocabulary has stayed fixed; the

49
00:01:55,761 --> 00:01:57,145
values have changed.

50
00:01:57,705 --> 00:01:59,607
Repetition can be useful evidence of

51
00:01:59,627 --> 00:02:02,841
topic. But raw counts keep growing, and

52
00:02:02,861 --> 00:02:04,916
long documents get more chances to

53
00:02:04,936 --> 00:02:05,998
accumulate them.

54
00:02:06,173 --> 00:02:08,267
We need a rule for how much another

55
00:02:08,287 --> 00:02:09,658
occurrence contributes.

56
00:02:10,569 --> 00:02:13,846
Term frequency looks inside a document.

57
00:02:14,021 --> 00:02:17,094
Inverse document frequency looks across

58
00:02:17,114 --> 00:02:18,008
the collection.

59
00:02:18,170 --> 00:02:20,380
Treatment occurs in two of our three

60
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:23,253
documents. Heart occurs in only one.

61
00:02:23,415 --> 00:02:25,702
Heart therefore distinguishes a smaller

62
00:02:25,722 --> 00:02:28,498
group and receives more rarity weight

63
00:02:28,518 --> 00:02:29,928
under the illustrated rule.

64
00:02:30,489 --> 00:02:32,939
The figure uses raw counts times the

65
00:02:32,959 --> 00:02:35,800
natural logarithm of collection size

66
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:37,835
divided by document frequency.

67
00:02:38,011 --> 00:02:40,078
The coordinates still mean words.

68
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:42,746
Adding collection statistics has not

69
00:02:42,766 --> 00:02:44,563
turned them into latent semantic

70
00:02:44,583 --> 00:02:45,529
dimensions.

71
00:02:46,428 --> 00:02:49,575
BM twenty five adds diminishing returns

72
00:02:49,595 --> 00:02:52,140
from repetition and adjusts term frequency

73
00:02:52,160 --> 00:02:54,279
evidence for document length, while

74
00:02:54,299 --> 00:02:56,765
retaining inverse document frequency.

75
00:02:56,928 --> 00:02:59,459
Our figure declares one standard parameter

76
00:02:59,479 --> 00:03:01,985
setting and computes the resulting term

77
00:03:02,005 --> 00:03:03,157
contributions.

78
00:03:03,698 --> 00:03:06,193
This is a comparison of representations,

79
00:03:06,343 --> 00:03:08,732
not a historical claim that one method was

80
00:03:08,752 --> 00:03:10,227
derived from another.

81
00:03:10,402 --> 00:03:15,343
Binary presence, raw counts, TF IDF and BM

82
00:03:15,363 --> 00:03:17,753
twenty five can all use vocabulary

83
00:03:17,773 --> 00:03:18,719
coordinates.

84
00:03:19,626 --> 00:03:22,633
A real vocabulary might contain millions

85
00:03:22,653 --> 00:03:25,636
of terms, but a short document activates

86
00:03:25,656 --> 00:03:27,104
only a few hundred.

87
00:03:27,279 --> 00:03:29,759
The implementation can store term and

88
00:03:29,779 --> 00:03:32,233
weight pairs for active coordinates.

89
00:03:32,786 --> 00:03:35,600
An inverted index lets a query jump to the

90
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:38,048
posting lists for its active terms and

91
00:03:38,068 --> 00:03:39,800
accumulate contributions.

92
00:03:39,963 --> 00:03:42,146
A dot product style mathematical

93
00:03:42,166 --> 00:03:45,149
description of BM twenty five does not

94
00:03:45,169 --> 00:03:48,242
imply that the engine scans dense vectors

95
00:03:48,262 --> 00:03:50,329
or runs nearest neighbour search.

96
00:03:51,237 --> 00:03:53,294
Return to the product claim: we use

97
00:03:53,314 --> 00:03:55,640
vectors. Ask what each coordinate

98
00:03:55,660 --> 00:03:58,591
represents, which values are active, how

99
00:03:58,611 --> 00:04:00,820
the weighting rule was obtained, and how

100
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:03,359
matching evidence becomes an eligible set

101
00:04:03,379 --> 00:04:04,299
or a score.

102
00:04:04,833 --> 00:04:07,024
The same numerical object can hold term

103
00:04:07,044 --> 00:04:09,858
presence, calculated lexical weights,

104
00:04:09,879 --> 00:04:12,797
recorded facts or learnt latent features.

105
00:04:12,959 --> 00:04:15,387
Calling it a vector settles none of those

106
00:04:15,407 --> 00:04:18,454
choices. In the next film, a dense vector

107
00:04:18,474 --> 00:04:21,161
fails a semantic test while a sparse one

108
00:04:21,181 --> 00:04:23,119
bridges a wording gap.
